~/opt, not installed system-wide; no Docker daemon on build2 or the Mac), 5.044 (Homebrew, Mac);
riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc (g6afcc4f6d) 16.1.0 (deps/); Yosys 0.33 (git sha1 2584903a060) + sv2v v0.0.13;
Vivado v2025.2 (64-bit); Sail 0.15, riscv-arch-test 6af53584, mise 2026.10.17; Spike 1.1.1-dev 2c300cd9
(riscv-isa-sim, softfloat submodule 32eb3295; dtc 1.7.0); riscv-dv 0d71c2b (8-riscv-dv flow at 84974af).
"off" = default build (FPGA_TIMING=0); "on" = every Verilator harness built with +define+SIGIL_FPGA_TIMING
+define+SIGIL_VRF_OREG (an extra makefile appending both defines to sim/Makefile's VFLAGS and VFLAGS_FAST, so
`make -C sim` builds every harness in the FPGA setting; the srammacro families then add their own defines on top).

