== Failures found in this round and fixed
1. CI break (Verilator 5.020). The gate harness's extra lint of sigil_csr/sigil_mmu with -GFPGA_TIMING=1
   failed on 5.020: %Warning-WIDTHTRUNC (a 32-bit 1 for the bit parameter) under -Wall. sim/Makefile builds
   csr_tb_fpga and mmu_tb_fpga the same way, and CI (core-regression.yml, apt 5.020) runs `make -C sim ... csr
   mmu ...`, so CI would have failed. Fix 3034a62: "-GFPGA_TIMING=1'b1"; 5.020 then builds and passes both
   (CI-parity run above). 5.048 and 5.044 never warned.
2. Default/ASIC logic not main's (sigil_mmu). The FPGA_TIMING=0 branches g_ireg_off / g_dreg_off computed
   main's port verdicts through the shared lookup_idx / port_result functions: equivalent (module proof) but a
   different structure, visible in the coarse stat of sigil_mmu (19,174 cells vs main's 19,255, standalone
   and inside the SoC file list). Fix 116c4a4: main's two always_comb blocks verbatim in the off branches, the one-hot fetch lookup
   and its check moved into g_ireg. Coarse sigil_mmu stat then equals main's (19,255).
Round-1 results before fix 2 (f4840f4 / 3034a62), all passing: lint 5.048 29/29; make test, core-test (off
3928 s, on 6739 s), socrtl, riscv-tests 123/123 in both settings; CI parity 5.020 (3034a62); ACT 2577/2578 in
both settings with the expected single failure; riscv-dv 100/100 on both sides.

